# =============================================================================
# .gitignore -- what this repository does NOT track, and why
# =============================================================================
# The rule throughout: RECORDS are tracked, COMPUTATIONS are not. Anything the
# pipeline can rebuild from `python3 run_all.py` is excluded. Anything that
# records a decision, a finding, or evidence is tracked, however small.
#
# NOTE ON SIZE: git has no size predicate, so "ignore any file over 50 MB"
# CANNOT be expressed here. Since 2026-09-23 the only files over 50 MB are the
# score and raw panels under cache/<tag>/, excluded by the cache/ rule below;
# they used to sit in results*/metrics/ as *_cache.csv. If a large file ever
# appears outside those directories, nothing here will stop it. A pre-commit hook is the only real guard; see the note at the bottom.

# A zero-byte file of unknown origin, referenced by nothing in the project; kept
# on disk but deliberately untracked.
permanent

# ----------------------------------------------------------------- environment
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.DS_Store
.idea/
*.iml

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- caches
# Derived data, rebuilt on demand: per-universe score and raw panels with their
# source-key sidecars, and the constituent symlink farms. See universes/registry.py
# (CACHE_DIR). Moved here from /tmp and data/raw/ on 2026-09-23.
cache/

# ------------------------------------------------------------ generated output
# Rebuilt in full by run_all.py. Includes every
# chart, every v2FINAL_* artefact, and the DAILY_LOG_*.txt forensic logs
# (regenerated by make_daily_log.py -- they are computations, not records).
results/metrics/
results74/metrics/
results_midcap150/metrics/
results_nifty100/metrics/
# THE SUPPLIER'S OTHER SIX, ALL ADDED AT ONCE ON 2026-09-18 -- five of them
# before the universe exists. Only n50 is registered today; the rule for the
# other five is written now so that bringing each one up cannot rediscover this
# the hard way. The first run of an un-ignored universe would offer its
# artefacts to git.
results_nifty50/metrics/
results_midcap50/metrics/
results_midcap100/metrics/
results_nifty200/metrics/
results_smallcap250/metrics/
results_nifty500/metrics/

# Derived from the score panels by run_all.py STEP 16; stale the moment those
# are rebuilt.
nautilus/data/*.parquet

# Engine output: orders.csv / fills.csv / positions.csv, per universe AND per arm.
nautilus/reports/

# The rebalance-cadence sweep's per-day audit streams: 61 MB across six files,
# regenerated by results/rebal_cadence_sweep.py. EXPERIMENTS.md records the shape
# (file list and row counts) so the reference in KNOWN_ISSUES.md still resolves to
# a description even when the directory is absent.
diagnostics/rebal_cadence_audit/

# Per-combination output: runs/{universe}/{arm}/. Written by run.py, one directory
# per (universe, arm), and rebuilt in full by `run.py --universe all --arm all`.
# Generated output like everything above it -- the numbers in it are reproducible
# from the panels, and its params.json records the git state that produced them.
runs/

# ------------------------------------------------------------ bulk price data
# ~396 MB of vendor OHLCV CSVs. Excluded for size, not for irrelevance -- the
# project cannot run without them, so they must be restored from the backup
# archive, not from this repository.
#
# WRITTEN AS `data/raw/*`, NOT `data/raw/`, AND THAT MATTERS.
#   git does not descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, so a `!` exception beneath
#   `data/raw/` is silently inert -- the negations below looked correct and
#   re-included nothing. Excluding the CONTENTS instead keeps the directory
#   traversable so the exceptions can take effect. Verified with
#   `git check-ignore` rather than assumed.
data/raw/*

# EXCEPTIONS UNDER data/raw/ -- SMALL, IRREPLACEABLE, NOT PRICE DATA.
#   These sit under data/raw/ only by historical accident. They are records, and
#   losing them would be unrecoverable: the NSE press-release PDFs they were
#   derived from were deleted in the 2026-08 cleanup, so they cannot be rebuilt.
#   Total 267 KB.
!data/raw/.gitkeep
!data/raw/membership_workbooks/
!data/raw/N100_Survivorship/
data/raw/N100_Survivorship/*
!data/raw/N100_Survivorship/index_membership_nifty100.csv

# =============================================================================
# EXTERNAL REFERENCE DOCUMENTS -- read by people, not by the pipeline
# =============================================================================
# TAX_AND_CHARGES.docx is the source document tax_util.py's section references
# quote. It is an INPUT TO THE READING, not an artefact this repository
# produces, and nothing imports or parses it.
#
# IT IS IGNORED RATHER THAN COMMITTED BECAUSE A STANDING UNTRACKED FILE COSTS A
# GATE. check_all.py's tree-clean reading was reported as "clean except
# data/reference/TAX_AND_CHARGES.docx" on four consecutive days. An exception
# that never clears stops being read as an exception and starts being read as
# the shape of the output, and the next genuinely untracked file arrives inside
# that blind spot. The .csv references above are tracked because they are
# pipeline inputs; a .docx is not.
data/reference/*.docx

# =============================================================================
# EXPLICITLY TRACKED -- listed so nobody adds a rule that swallows them
# =============================================================================
# Not ignored by anything above; recorded here as intent.
#
#   experiments/                       the entire experiment record, including
#                                      EXPERIMENTS.md, all five preregs,
#                                      sizing_test.py, and the two REPORT.txt
#                                      files restored from backup on 2026-08-22
#   data/reference/*.csv               nse_press_release_manifest.csv,
#                                      nse_symbol_renames.csv,
#                                      nse_circulars_2019_2026.csv (9.4 MB)
#                                      -- .csv only. data/reference/*.docx is
#                                      ignored, see the section above it.
#   data/nse_trading_calendar.csv      pipeline input, STEP 0 rebuilds it but it
#                                      is small and deterministic
#   nautilus/NAUTILUS_STATUS.md        port status and its correction history
#   SURVIVORSHIP_README.md
#   diagnostics/                       every findings .txt, the membership
#                                      rebuild, STATUS.md, INVENTORY.csv, and
#                                      the two NSE tick-size circular PDFs
#   run_*_log.txt, run_log.txt         pipeline run logs; three of them are the
#                                      cited evidence for the EWMA experiment
#                                      (run_all_ewma_log.txt, ewma2, fresh)
#   nautilus/run_full_log.txt
#
# A PRE-COMMIT SIZE GUARD, if you want one later:
#   git config --local core.hooksPath .githooks
#   then a hook rejecting any staged blob over 50 MB. Not installed; noted so
#   the gap above is a known gap rather than an assumed protection.
forensic_snapshot_*/
forensic_snapshot_*/
pre_repoint_baseline/
superseded_tradeable_*/
